FOUND s495f (task #2051's breaking-case probes, scratch/s495f/p-qr5.pl), PRE-EXISTING (identical on 3d9b3712).
    package Over; use overload '""' => sub { "OVER" }; package main;
    my $o = bless qr/z/, "Over";
    print "$o ", ("xzx" =~ $o ? "match" : "nomatch"), " ", ("OVER" =~ $o ? "match" : "nomatch"), "\n";
  perl 5.40.3:  OVER nomatch match      (the pattern used is the overloaded stringification "OVER")
  PCL:          OVER match nomatch      (the compiled regex is used directly)
Rare shape (an overloaded class wrapping a qr).  WHERE: the match-operand path takes a p-regex-match payload as the pattern without asking the invocant's `""` overload -- the sibling of #119/#402 (s///, tr/// match SOURCES run the `""` overload).  A fix must not put a class check on the hot match path: ask only when the box carries a class (the slot is nil for every unblessed qr).  Low priority.
